    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d564">

                <pb facs="0734" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Food Administrator’s File</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative of the Food
                        Administration</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Taylor</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Food Administrator</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hoover</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 16, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>… Policy established and accepted that exportable North American wheat is limited
                    to 132,000,000 bushels. Allies would prefer to have this all within three
                    months. Expect to import 2,000,000 tons each Argentine and India. In the event
                    of hiatus prior to Argentine deliveries would it be possible to borrow from
                    United States 1,000,000 tons wheat and replace later from the Argentine
                    Republic? Attempting to increase use of oatmeal. Wire definite figure on
                    exportable surplus of rye and barley fit for human consumption. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taylor</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
